From: steamac <steamac@fxgam.es>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MSL: zero robust loads in temporaries where they are assigned

STEAMAC-CB (two events) and STEAMAC-CF (1.9.15, M1/M2): MoltenVK shader
library compile failed, "162:24 use of undeclared identifier '_154'". A
uniform-buffer load in an inner loop (`_156 = cb5.m[min(_154, ...)].y`,
`_154 = _122 + 256u` a temporary of the loop) is used after the loop, so
SPIRV-Cross hoists `_156` out of the loop and assigns it there. With
robustBufferAccess2 the OpLoad handler then replaced the expression of the
load, already a temporary, with `(uint(_154) < size ? _156 : 0)`: every use
re-evaluated the bounds check, after the loop naming `_154`, out of scope
(and in scope, with the values its operands had at that use).

When the load went into a temporary (unpacked, of the logical type), zero it
right after its assignment, `_156 = cond ? _156 : 0;`, where the operands of
the check are those of the load, and leave its uses as the temporary.
Forwarded loads keep the select in their expression; array loads keep their
`if (!cond) { t = {}; }`.

Regression: host/moltenvk/repro/sentry-cb-robust-hoist.sh <spirv-cross>:
valid SPIR-V with a robust uniform load in a loop, its index a temporary of
the loop, used after it reproduces `use of undeclared identifier` before;
after, MSL 2.4 and 3.0 compile with and without robustness, and the GPU
reads 0 after the loop for an out-of-bounds index (the unguarded value runs
the loop on) and the loaded values in bounds. Of SPIRV-Cross's MSL test
shaders (344 GLSL, 219 assembly) run with robustBufferAccess2, only
load-packed-no-forwarding-4 changes: its two temporaries are zeroed at their
assignment instead of at each use. sentry-msl.sh, sentry-b6-continue.sh and
sentry-8j-projected.sh pass.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 spirv_msl.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/spirv_msl.cpp b/spirv_msl.cpp
index b41d6e7..94b698b 100644
--- a/spirv_msl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_msl.cpp
@@ -11573,6 +11573,15 @@ void CompilerMSL::emit_instruction(const Instruction &instruction)
 				statement(to_name(id), " = {};");
 				end_scope();
 			}
+			else if (expr && expr->expression == to_name(id))
+			{
+				// The load went into a temporary (unpacked, of the logical type), which can be hoisted
+				// out of a loop and used after it. Zero it where it is assigned: the bounds check names
+				// temporaries of this block, which a use after the loop would not see (STEAMAC-CB/CF,
+				// `use of undeclared identifier`), and would read with their values at that use.
+				statement(to_name(id), " = ", info.bounds_check_condition, " ? ", to_name(id), " : ",
+				          robust_zero_expression(get<SPIRType>(result_type)), ";");
+			}
 			else if (expr)
 			{
 				// A forwarded load is still in the physical layout of the buffer (packed vectors and
